            <ArticleTitle>Rash, abdominal pain and hyponatraemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>184-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hypertriglyceridaemia is a rare precipitant of acute pancreatitis. We present a patient with acute pancreatitis and hyponatraemia in association with severe hyperlipidaemia, predominantly hypertriglyceridaemia. The patient was successfully treated with plasma exchange therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
